35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found it! Chasing money takes six hours a month, but yearly collection is only one hour. That is so much easier!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Minato, that confirms my suspicion. The ledger shows seventy percent of costs are fixed, regardless of attendance. We must structure fees to cover those fixed costs reliably, not chase variable income.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, the bank statements confirm the strain. A third of renewals needed reminders, and several requested monthly installments. We need a structure that respects that reality, not just the fixed costs.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"@Minato, six hours a month is brutal! But my sign-in tally is worse. A quarter of us do two-thirds of the work, and eighteen people never show up. How do we charge ghosts?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, ghosts don’t pay, but they don’t work either. The rota confirms the same nine people do everything. We need to price that labor, not just the rent.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, one hour is so much better! But if we only collect once a year, will people forget? I want to make sure the next person isn't lonely with the books.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Minato, forgetting is a risk, but chasing is a certainty. We must prioritize the one-hour model to eliminate the six-hour monthly burden.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, I agree. The bank statements show people struggle with large lump sums. A single yearly payment is cleaner, but we must ensure it is affordable enough that nobody defaults.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minako, affordability is key! But my winter social notes show people hesitate because they don’t know what they’re paying for. We need transparency to stop that last-minute anxiety.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minako, affordability is a luxury for the ghosts. The same nine people carry the physical load. We must price that labor, not just the rent.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@May, eighteen people not showing up is sad. But if we collect once a year, the books are simple. I hope that helps the next person feel less lonely.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"May, transparency is essential, but it cannot replace reliable revenue. We must secure the fixed costs first. I will examine the sign-up records to verify who actually commits.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@May, transparency is vital, but it cannot replace reliable revenue. We must secure the fixed costs first. I will examine the sign-up records to verify who actually commits.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, I hear you, but transparency isn't just nice-to-have! If people don't know what they're paying for, they hesitate. I need to see the taster forms to understand that hesitation.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, transparency is a band-aid. The rota proves the same nine people do the work. We must price that labor, not just the rent.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, I agree. One hour is so much better than six! I hope the next person feels less lonely with the books. I am ready to see the options.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"Minato, the data is clear. We must eliminate the monthly chasing burden. I am ready to evaluate the options against the fixed cost baseline.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,I am ready to evaluate the options. The data confirms the strain on both the treasurer and the members. We must balance reliability with affordability.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"I’m ready to see the options! But I need to know if they fix the hesitation. If people don’t feel they belong, no fee structure works.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,I am ready. The data is undeniable. We must stop subsidizing ghosts with the labor of the nine. Let us see the options.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
